    "https://western.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WESTERN/job/USA-Colorado-Remote/Post-Award-Grants-Analyst_R938": {
      "title": "Post Award Grants Analyst",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nPosition Summary: Job Description: Position: Western Colorado University invites applications for the full-time position of Post-Award Grants Analyst.   The position reports to the Controller, works closely with the Accounting department, the Pre-Award Specialist, and Department administrative staff , and is responsible for the management of all University grants, from setup to closeout.   This job is eligible for remote work. Responsibilities:  The Post-Award Grants Analyst is responsible for administering funding from federal, state, and private grants/sponsored projects awarded to the university, ensuring the institution meets compliance and financial reporting requirements. This position will also work closely with department finance, providing data analysis to help guide them in their decision-making throughout the grant.   Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and one year working in an accounting-related field, which may be substituted for an advanced finance or accounting degree. Preferred Qualifications: A degree in finance or accounting, one year of post-award grants management, Workday experience, and Excel data analysis experience. Compensation: $50,000-60,000. This position is FLSA exempt.   Western offers an excellent benefits package including shared premiums for a comprehensive health insurance plan, dental insurance, retirement plan, life insurance, and other insurance options. After one year of employment, Western provides free tuition for dependents enrolled full time in undergraduate programs for up to four years. Application Procedure:  Apply online at www.Western.edu/jobs . Required attachments for online application include a letter of application addressed to Justin Weigle, resume, and contact information for three references. In compliance with the Colorado Job Application Fairness Act, in any materials you submit, you may redact or remove age-identifying information such as age, date of birth, or dates of school attendance or graduation. You will not be penalized for redacting or removing this information. Please direct questions to the search committee chair at jweigle@western.edu . Application deadline is October 18th. Additional Information on Western and Gunnison/Crested Butte Western Colorado University is a public institution with an enrollment of ~3,700 students. 47% of students are undergraduates, 33% are graduate students, and 80% receive some form of financial aid. Western students represent 17 countries, 50 states, and almost every county in Colorado. With an average class size of 17, Western’s faculty and staff share a strong commitment to personalized, rigorous, and immersive education. Visit  http://www.western.edu  to learn more about the university.   Western Colorado University is located in Gunnison, Colorado, about 200 miles southwest of Denver amidst over 2 million acres of public land and a vibrant ranching community. The Gunnison valley provides robust cultural programming and exceptional outdoor recreation. A network of dedicated community organizations enrich the lives of many in the tight-knit community. Living in the valley , one appreciates a vibrant culture of festivals, exhibitions, performances, wellness activities, and more. In the winter, many enjoy in skiing at Crested Butte Mountain Resort and along dozens of miles of cross-country trails. In the summer, bikers, hikers, and runners explore 750-plus miles of singletrack trails, while others delight in fishing, boating, and paddleboarding at Blue Mesa Reservoir or on the Gunnison River and its tributaries. Pre-K-12 students are served by the highly-ranked Gunnison Watershed School District .   An Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability/vets. WESTERN COLORADO UNIVERSITY IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER INCLUDING DISABILITY/VETERANS It is the ongoing policy and practice of Western Colorado University to provide equal opportunity in employment to all employees and applicants.  No person shall be discriminated against in any condition of employment because of age (40 and over), color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, military or veteran status, national origin, ancestry, race, religion, creed, sex, sexual orientation, gender expression, marital status, or any other applicable status protected by federal, state, or local law. ADAAA ACCOMMODATIONS: Western Colorado University is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. As part of this commitment, Western will assist individuals who have a disability with any reasonable accommodation requests related to employment, including completing the application process, interviewing, completing any pre-employment testing, participating in the employee selection process, and/or performing essential job functions where the requested accommodation does not impose an undue hardship. If you have a disability and require reasonable accommodation to ensure you have a positive experience applying or interviewing for this position, please direct your inquiries to the Office of Human Resources at HR@western.edu or (970) 943-3140."
    },
    "https://western.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WESTERN/job/Gunnison-CO/Assistant-Director-of-Admissions_R943": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Admissions",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nPosition Summary: Job Description: Position: Western Colorado University invites applications for the full-time position of Assistant Director of Admissions.   The position reports to the Director of Admissions, works closely with admissions, marketing, and financial aid , and is responsible for operational leadership, capability development, and strategic execution to support the Admissions Team and the broader Enrollment Division. This on-campus or remote position in the Front Range is responsible for managing their assigned territory, supervising and training admissions counselors, student ambassadors and other support staff, and assisting with budget management, travel planning and operational processes within the admissions office. Responsibilities: The Assistant Director of Admissions will be responsible for the following. Lead Recruitment and Territory Management Develop and execute recruitment strategies to achieve enrollment goals within assigned territories. Conduct high school visits, college fairs, virtual events, and other outreach activities. Build and maintain relationships with counselors, community partners, students, and families. Manage Admissions Operations and Application Review Evaluate applications and make admissions decisions in accordance with university policies. Ensure accurate management of applicant records and admissions workflows within CRM and student information systems. Support process improvements and compliance with institutional, state, and federal regulations. Support Strategic Enrollment Planning and Cross-Campus Collaboration Analyze recruitment and enrollment data to inform decision-making and improve outcomes. Collaborate with Financial Aid, Marketing, Academic Affairs, Athletics, and Student Success partners to advance enrollment objectives. Contribute to departmental planning, assessment, and special projects while serving as a member of the admissions leadership team.   Minimum Qualifications: Below are the minimum qualifications. Bachelor’s degree 2+ years of proven experience in higher education, business, marketing and/or sales Experience managing a team Valid driver’s license Ability to multi-task, prioritize duties Excellent communication skills, both written and verbal Skilled at leading teams to meet or exceed objectives Ability to remain a strategic thinker, problem solver, and process innovator Ability to work effectively cross- functionally, in a matrix, integrated work/leadership environment Proficient computer skills in Word, Excel, CRM software and use of Internet Ability to work long days or weekends during the peak admission season and to travel out of state when needed Preferred Qualifications: Please see preferred qualifications below. Master’s degree Compensation: $57,000-61,000. This position is FLSA exempt. Western offers an excellent benefits package including shared premiums for a comprehensive health insurance plan, dental insurance, retirement plan, life insurance, and other insurance options. After one year of employment, Western provides free tuition for dependents enrolled full time in undergraduate programs for up to four years. Application Procedure:  Apply online at www.Western.edu/jobs . Required attachments for online application include a letter of application addressed to Chase Watts, Director of Admissions, resume, and contact information for three references. In compliance with the Colorado Job Application Fairness Act, in any materials you submit, you may redact or remove age-identifying information such as age, date of birth, or dates of school attendance or graduation. You will not be penalized for redacting or removing this information. Please direct questions to the search committee chair at abevan@western.edu. Application deadline is October 31st, 2026. Additional Information on Western and Gunnison/Crested Butte Western Colorado University is a public institution with an enrollment of ~3,700 students. 47% of students are undergraduates, 33% are graduate students, and 80% receive some form of financial aid. Western students represent 17 countries, 50 states, and almost every county in Colorado. With an average class size of 17, Western’s faculty and staff share a strong commitment to personalized, rigorous, and immersive education. Visit  http://www.western.edu  to learn more about the university.   Western Colorado University is located in Gunnison, Colorado, about 200 miles southwest of Denver amidst over 2 million acres of public land and a vibrant ranching community. The Gunnison valley provides robust cultural programming and exceptional outdoor recreation. A network of dedicated community organizations enrich the lives of many in the tight-knit community. Living in the valley , one appreciates a vibrant culture of festivals, exhibitions, performances, wellness activities, and more. In the winter, many enjoy in skiing at Crested Butte Mountain Resort and along dozens of miles of cross-country trails. In the summer, bikers, hikers, and runners explore 750-plus miles of singletrack trails, while others delight in fishing, boating, and paddleboarding at Blue Mesa Reservoir or on the Gunnison River and its tributaries. Pre-K-12 students are served by the highly-ranked Gunnison Watershed School District .   An Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability/vets.   WESTERN COLORADO UNIVERSITY IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER INCLUDING DISABILITY/VETERANS It is the ongoing policy and practice of Western Colorado University to provide equal opportunity in employment to all employees and applicants.  No person shall be discriminated against in any condition of employment because of age (40 and over), color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, military or veteran status, national origin, ancestry, race, religion, creed, sex, sexual orientation, gender expression, marital status, or any other applicable status protected by federal, state, or local law. ADAAA ACCOMMODATIONS: Western Colorado University is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. As part of this commitment, Western will assist individuals who have a disability with any reasonable accommodation requests related to employment, including completing the application process, interviewing, completing any pre-employment testing, participating in the employee selection process, and/or performing essential job functions where the requested accommodation does not impose an undue hardship. If you have a disability and require reasonable accommodation to ensure you have a positive experience applying or interviewing for this position, please direct your inquiries to the Office of Human Resources at HR@western.edu or (970) 943-3140."
    },
    "https://western.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WESTERN/job/Gunnison-CO/Tenure-Track-Faculty-in-Finance_R950": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Faculty in Finance",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nPosition Summary: Job Description: Western Colorado University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position in Finance in the School of Business. We seek a dynamic teacher-scholar who is committed to excellent undergraduate teaching, student-centered learning, professional preparation, and applied, career-connected education. This is an in-person, on-campus position on Western’s vibrant residential campus in Gunnison, Colorado.   Finance is central to business education and to understanding how organizations, industries, and economies create, allocate, and sustain value. At Western, finance connects across our curriculum and distinctive areas of study—from the experience economy and energy industry to economics, entrepreneurship, real estate, and the broader business disciplines—providing students with the financial knowledge and analytical capabilities essential to informed decision-making and effective leadership.   The successful candidate will join the School of Business at an exciting time of growth and innovation and will contribute broadly to finance education across our programs. An important component of this growth is the development of a new Certified Financial Planner (CFP) educational pathway designed to prepare students for careers in financial planning and related financial services fields.   We especially welcome candidates who can contribute expertise in areas such as financial planning, investments, portfolio management, retirement planning, insurance, estate planning, taxation, personal finance, corporate finance, or related areas of finance.   The standard teaching load is 24 credit hours per academic year. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate finance courses and other courses aligned with their expertise and School needs. The successful candidate will also have the opportunity to collaborate with School of Business faculty and external partners in the development and implementation of Western’s new CFP curriculum and its alignment with CFP Board educational requirements.   Western values faculty who connect classroom learning with professional practice. The successful candidate will have opportunities to engage students through applied learning experiences such as internships, investment and financial analysis projects, community-based learning, research, case competitions, industry partnerships, and other career-connected learning opportunities. Faculty may also participate in Western’s innovative Western Watershed General Education program and First-Year Seminar Headwaters courses.   The School of Business serves more than 325 students across its majors and minors. Students can earn degrees in Business Administration and Economics, with emphases including energy management, finance, management, and marketing. Our programs combine rigorous academic preparation with applied learning, close faculty mentorship, industry engagement, and opportunities for students to bridge theory and practice.   The School is expanding opportunities in finance through curricular innovation, professional and industry partnerships, community engagement, and applied learning. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to help shape this growth and contribute to preparing students for careers across financial planning, investment management, banking, corporate finance, entrepreneurship, and other areas in which financial knowledge and decision-making are essential.   Western supports its faculty by fostering a collaborative and innovative academic community. Our Teaching and Learning Center (TLC) engages faculty, staff, and administrators in cross-campus initiatives designed to strengthen teaching and learning through diverse expertise, innovation, and continuous improvement. The Professional Activity Fund (PAF) provides financial support for faculty engaged in research, conference participation, grant writing, professional development, and other scholarly or creative activities, with three application opportunities each year.   Western’s faculty are teacher-scholars who contribute meaningfully to their disciplines, the University, our community, and beyond. We seek candidates who will actively support Western’s institutional mission and strategic priorities, including:   Delivering rigorous, engaging, and student-centered undergraduate education Participating in Western’s innovative Western Watershed General Education program Promoting student success, wellness, inclusion, and belonging Collaborating within and across disciplines to grow enrollment and deepen student engagement Expanding applied and career-connected learning and professional pathways Building relationships with employers, alumni, industry partners, and professional organizations Contributing through teaching, scholarship, advising, service, and engagement to the continued growth of the School of Business   Learn more about the department at: https://western.edu/department/school-of-business/   QUALIFICATIONS   Required Qualifications:   A Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree in Finance, Financial Planning, Business Administration with a finance concentration, or a closely related field is required. ABD candidates will be considered for appointment, with completion of the terminal degree required for tenure. Candidates must demonstrate: A commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching and student-centered education Academic preparation to teach finance and related courses at the undergraduate level Potential for continued scholarship, research, professional engagement, or other scholarly activity appropriate to the discipline A commitment to advising, mentoring, and supporting students from a broad range of backgrounds and educational experiences An ability to integrate technology and contemporary financial tools into instruction An ability and willingness to teach in multiple instructional modalities, including in-person, online, and hybrid formats A willingness to contribute to university and professional service Collegiality, collaboration, and professional flexibility   Preferred Qualifications:   Teaching and/or professional expertise in one or more areas of finance, including investments, corporate finance, financial planning, portfolio management, personal finance, banking, real estate finance, or related fields Professional or industry experience that strengthens the connection between finance education and contemporary business practice Experience developing innovative courses, curricula, certificates, academic programs, or interdisciplinary learning opportunities Experience building partnerships with financial institutions, businesses, professional organizations, employers, alumni, or community organizations Experience incorporating applied learning, financial technology, data analytics, artificial intelligence, simulations, case studies, or industry projects into finance education A record of engaging students in internships, research, professional development, competitions, community-based learning, or other career-connected experiences Certified Financial Planner™ (CFP®) certification or another relevant professional finance credential   SALARY AND BENEFITS   The annualized salary range for this position depends on incoming rank (assistant professor or associate professor), qualifications, and experience.    Assistant Professor - $95,000 to $105,000 Associate Professor - $105,000 to $120,000                                                 Western offers an excellent benefits package, including shared premiums for comprehensive health insurance, dental insurance, retirement benefits, life insurance, and additional insurance options. After one year of employment, Western provides free tuition for eligible dependents enrolled full-time in undergraduate programs for up to four years.   START DATE: August 16, 2027     APPLICATION: Apply online at www.western.edu/jobs .  Required attachments to the application include: Letter of application, curriculum vitae, evidence of successful teaching and mentoring, evidence of successful scholarly or creative activity, and a reference list with names and contact information of three references, including from a current supervisor.                                     In compliance with the Colorado Job Application Fairness Act, in any materials you submit, you may redact or remove age-identifying information such as age, date of birth, or dates of school attendance or graduation. You will not be penalized for redacting or removing this information.   Please direct questions to Dr. Kevin Nelson, email: knelson@western.edu    APPLICATION DEADLINE: November 1, 2026. Review of applications will begin immediately.     Additional Information on Western and Gunnison/Crested Butte   Western Colorado University is a public institution with an enrollment of ~3,700 students. 47% of students are undergraduates, 33% are graduate students, and 80% receive some form of financial aid. Western students represent 17 countries, 50 states, and almost every county in Colorado. With an average class size of 17, Western’s faculty and staff share a strong commitment to personalized, rigorous, and immersive education. Visit  http://www.western.edu  to learn more about the university.   Western Colorado University is located in Gunnison, Colorado, about 200 miles southwest of Denver amidst over 2 million acres of public land and a vibrant ranching community. The Gunnison valley provides robust cultural programming and exceptional outdoor recreation. A network of dedicated community organizations enrich the lives of many in the tight-knit community. Living in the valley , one appreciates a vibrant culture of festivals, exhibitions, performances, wellness activities, and more. In the winter, many enjoy skiing at Crested Butte Mountain Resort and along dozens of miles of cross-country trails. In the summer, bikers, hikers, and runners explore 750-plus miles of singletrack trails, while others delight in fishing, boating, and paddleboarding at Blue Mesa Reservoir or on the Gunnison River and its tributaries. Pre-K-12 students are served by the highly-ranked Gunnison Watershed School District .   Western Colorado University encourages qualified candidates from all identities, backgrounds, and abilities to apply. Western is an equal opportunity employer committed to building inclusive, innovative work environments with employees who reflect our communities and enthusiastically serve them. Therefore, in all aspects of the employment process, we provide employment opportunities to all qualified applicants in accordance with applicable law.   An Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability/vets.   WESTERN COLORADO UNIVERSITY IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER INCLUDING DISABILITY/VETERANS It is the ongoing policy and practice of Western Colorado University to provide equal opportunity in employment to all employees and applicants.  No person shall be discriminated against in any condition of employment because of age (40 and over), color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, military or veteran status, national origin, ancestry, race, religion, creed, sex, sexual orientation, gender expression, marital status, or any other applicable status protected by federal, state, or local law. ADAAA ACCOMMODATIONS: Western Colorado University is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. As part of this commitment, Western will assist individuals who have a disability with any reasonable accommodation requests related to employment, including completing the application process, interviewing, completing any pre-employment testing, participating in the employee selection process, and/or performing essential job functions where the requested accommodation does not impose an undue hardship. If you have a disability and require reasonable accommodation to ensure you have a positive experience applying or interviewing for this position, please direct your inquiries to the Office of Human Resources at HR@western.edu or (970) 943-3140."
    },
    "https://western.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WESTERN/job/Gunnison-CO/Tenure-Track-Faculty-in-Sustainable-Tourism-and-Hospitality_R949": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Faculty in Sustainable Tourism and Hospitality",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nPosition Summary: Job Description: Western Colorado University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position in Sustainable Tourism and Hospitality.  We seek a dynamic teacher-scholar who is committed to student-centered learning, professional preparation, and inclusive, interdisciplinary education. This is an in-person, on-campus position on our vibrant residential campus in Gunnison, Colorado. Located in the heart of Colorado’s world-renowned tourism and outdoor recreation region, Western offers students a one-of-a-kind environment to learn, lead, and grow. Surrounded by top ski resorts, national parks, boutique lodges, and adventure tourism hubs, students gain direct access to the very settings where hospitality excellence is both expected and tested — and these same lessons apply on a global scale. Students gain expertise in key areas such as marketing, human resources, real estate, finance, data analytics, and facilities management. The standard teaching load is 24 credit hours per academic year. The successful candidate will deliver engaging, well-designed courses in tourism and hospitality, including an introductory course, Resort Operations and Management, as well as other courses aligned with their expertise and departmental needs. The successful candidate will also work with faculty in the Business School to reimagine this program toward experience management (including sports, entertainment, and more).  We especially value faculty who engage students in high-impact practices such as internships, research, community-based learning, and who participate in our Western Watershed General Education and First-Year Seminar Headwaters courses. We prepare students for a livelihood based on their values and aid students in gaining post-graduate opportunities.   The School of Business serves over 325 students across its majors and minors. Students can earn a degree in Business Administration and Economics, with emphases in energy management, finance, management, and marketing, combining rigorous academic preparation with high-impact experiential learning.   Western supports its faculty by fostering a collaborative and innovative academic community. Our Teaching and Learning Center (TLC) actively engages faculty, staff, and administrators in cross-campus initiatives designed to reimagine WCU’s educational landscape—rooted in diverse expertise and committed to continuous growth. The Professional Activity Fund (PAF) provides financial support for faculty engaged in research, artistic projects, grant writing, and other scholarly or creative activities, with three application opportunities each year. Western’s faculty are teacher-scholars who contribute meaningfully to their discipline, the campus, our community, and beyond. We seek candidates who will actively support our institutional mission and strategic priorities, including:   Participating in our innovative Western Watershed General Education program Promoting wellness, inclusion, and belonging Collaborating within and across disciplines to grow enrollment and deepen student engagement Expanding career-connected learning and professional pathways   Learn more about the department at: https://western.edu/department/school-of-business/   QUALIFICATIONS: A Ph.D. or similar degree in the tourism and/or hospitality areas or related field is required.  ABD considered for hire, completed degree required for tenure.  Candidates must have a demonstrated commitment to undergraduate education, excellence in teaching, and willingness to work with and be sensitive to the educational needs of all students. Also required is the ability for research and professional development within a related field of study, and experience in university service.  Candidates must also be able to use technology in instructional delivery, including the ability to teach online and hybrid courses. Collegiality and professional flexibility are sought in the successful candidate.   SALARY/BENEFITS:  The annualized salary range for this position depends on incoming rank (assistant professor or associate professor), qualifications, and experience.    Assistant Professor - $90,000 to $100,000 Associate Professor - $100,000 to $110,000                                                 Western offers an excellent benefits package, including shared premiums for comprehensive health insurance, dental insurance, retirement benefits, life insurance, and additional insurance options. After one year of employment, Western provides free tuition for eligible dependents enrolled full-time in undergraduate programs for up to four years.   START DATE:  January 6, 2027 or August 16, 2027   APPLICATION:   Apply online at www.western.edu/jobs .  Required attachments to the application include: Letter of application, curriculum vitae, evidence of successful teaching and mentoring, evidence of successful scholarly or creative activity, and a reference list with names and contact information of three references, including from a current supervisor.                                     In compliance with the Colorado Job Application Fairness Act, in any materials you submit, you may redact or remove age-identifying information such as age, date of birth, or dates of school attendance or graduation. You will not be penalized for redacting or removing this information.   Please direct questions to Dr. Kevin Nelson, email: knelson@western.edu    APPLICATION DEADLINE: November 1, 2026. Review of applications will begin immediately.   Additional Information on Western and Gunnison/Crested Butte Western Colorado University is a public institution with an enrollment of ~3,700 students. 47% of students are undergraduates, 33% are graduate students, and 80% receive some form of financial aid. Western students represent 17 countries, 50 states, and almost every county in Colorado. With an average class size of 17, Western’s faculty and staff share a strong commitment to personalized, rigorous, and immersive education. Visit  http://www.western.edu  to learn more about the university. Western Colorado University is located in Gunnison, Colorado, about 200 miles southwest of Denver amidst over 2 million acres of public land and a vibrant ranching community. The Gunnison valley provides robust cultural programming and exceptional outdoor recreation. A network of dedicated community organizations enrich the lives of many in the tight-knit community. Living in the valley , one appreciates a vibrant culture of festivals, exhibitions, performances, wellness activities, and more. In the winter, many enjoy skiing at Crested Butte Mountain Resort and along dozens of miles of cross-country trails. In the summer, bikers, hikers, and runners explore 750-plus miles of singletrack trails, while others delight in fishing, boating, and paddleboarding at Blue Mesa Reservoir or on the Gunnison River and its tributaries. Pre-K-12 students are served by the highly-ranked Gunnison Watershed School District . Western Colorado University encourages qualified candidates from all identities, backgrounds, and abilities to apply. Western is an equal opportunity employer committed to building inclusive, innovative work environments with employees who reflect our communities and enthusiastically serve them. Therefore, in all aspects of the employment process, we provide employment opportunities to all qualified applicants in accordance with applicable law.   An Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability/vets. WESTERN COLORADO UNIVERSITY IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER INCLUDING DISABILITY/VETERANS It is the ongoing policy and practice of Western Colorado University to provide equal opportunity in employment to all employees and applicants.  No person shall be discriminated against in any condition of employment because of age (40 and over), color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, military or veteran status, national origin, ancestry, race, religion, creed, sex, sexual orientation, gender expression, marital status, or any other applicable status protected by federal, state, or local law. ADAAA ACCOMMODATIONS: Western Colorado University is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. As part of this commitment, Western will assist individuals who have a disability with any reasonable accommodation requests related to employment, including completing the application process, interviewing, completing any pre-employment testing, participating in the employee selection process, and/or performing essential job functions where the requested accommodation does not impose an undue hardship. If you have a disability and require reasonable accommodation to ensure you have a positive experience applying or interviewing for this position, please direct your inquiries to the Office of Human Resources at HR@western.edu or (970) 943-3140."
    },
    "https://western.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WESTERN/job/Gunnison-CO/Security-I_R951": {
      "title": "Security I",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nPay Range: $17.38 - $24.32 Position Summary: Job Description: This position is scheduled for night shifts (8:00 pm – 6:00 am) and is eligible for shift differential pay, meaning the pay is an additional 14% per hour (up to $22.10 per hour) for weeknights and 20% more per hour (up to $23.26 per hour) for weekends. Salary Note: Although the full salary range for this position is provided, appointments are typically made at or near the range minimum. DEPARTMENT INFORMATION: Western Colorado University is a residential, public university with an enrollment of 3,000 students who come from across Colorado and all fifty states. Faculty and staff members share a strong commitment to personalized education with the liberal arts as its core. They are student-oriented, collegial, energetic, and engaged in the campus and community. The curriculum provides flexibility where experiential learning and interdisciplinary approaches are valued. The University is located in Gunnison, Colorado, a rural community 200 miles southwest of Denver. At an elevation of 7,700 feet in the southern Rocky Mountains, the Gunnison Valley provides exceptional year-round outdoor recreational opportunities. Employees have chosen Western because of the quality of life combined with rewarding careers. To learn more about the University, visit  www.western.edu . For a glimpse of Western's wonderful location in the Gunnison Valley, visit  gunnisoncrestedbutte.com . EMPLOYEE BENEFITS: Colorado PERA retirement Voluntary participation in 401(k), 457, and 403(b) retirement plans Medical, dental, and vision insurance (with generous employer premium contributions) Basic life insurance coverage (at no cost) Optional life insurance for employees and their families Short-term disability coverage (at no cost) Optional long-term disability coverage Flexible spending plans Employer contributions to a qualified Health Savings Account 11 paid state holidays per year Paid vacation and sick leave An annual campus health fair with free biometric/blood screenings, free flu shots, and other free screening services available Discounted memberships to the campus fieldhouse and fitness center Employee and dependent tuition benefits after one year of employment DESCRIPTION OF JOB: Western Colorado University Security Services provides a safe and secure environment for students, faculty, staff, and visitors on Western's campus. This is accomplished through a community-friendly approach, visibility of security personnel, 24-hour accessibility, roving patrols, and cooperation with all local emergency agencies.     JOB DUTIES Patrol campus grounds by vehicle or on foot to protect state and personal property Walk through and patrol buildings to identify safety hazards and verify safe conditions Respond to parking and traffic violations on campus; patrol parking lots to ensure safety of persons and vehicles Document incidents that occur and actions taken during shift As needed, notify local law enforcement of incidents and participate with law enforcement during investigation of criminal activity Participate in campus events to ensure safety while conducting crowd and traffic control Assist with campus/building/facility maintenance; contact appropriate personnel when mechanical or physical problems are discovered/identified during shift; document work orders submitted or actions taken for repairs In the event of a major emergency, integrate into an incident command structure and follow the emergency operations plan MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS None PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Excellent verbal and written communication skills Customer service skills Ability to handle emergencies calmly and efficiently Attention to detail and ability to observe surroundings Excellent problem solving skills Experience working with and communicating with emergency services Strong communication and interpersonal skills Ability to work in a team environment High school diploma or GED Prior State service in a position requiring similar job knowledge, skills, or abilities When submitting the initial employment application/materials for this position, applicants may redact information that identifies their age, date of birth, or dates of attendance at or graduation from an education institution or program. FOR CURRENT OR FORMER EMPLOYEES OF THE STATE OF COLORADO: Per the requirements of the Step Pay Program implemented on July 1, 2024, any State employee must be paid a rate that is equal to or greater than the appropriate step pay rate within their classification’s pay range based on completed years in their current class series as of June 30.  All current and former State employees must ensure that your entire work history within the State Classified System, including at Institutions of Higher Education, is indicated in your application so that your time-in-series can be calculated accurately.   CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Must be a Colorado Resident at the time of application The selected candidate must pass a criminal background check The selected candidate must have a valid regular Colorado Driver's License APPEAL RIGHTS If you receive notice that you have been eliminated from consideration for this position, you may file an appeal with the State Personnel Board or request a review by the State Personnel Director. An appeal or review must be submitted on the official appeal form, signed by you or your representative. This form must be delivered to the State Personnel Board by email (dpa_state.personnelboard@state.co.us), postmarked in US Mail or hand delivered (1525 Sherman Street, 4th Floor, Denver CO 80203), or faxed (303.866.5038) within ten (10) calendar days from your receipt of notice or acknowledgement of the department’s action. For more information about the appeals process, the official appeal form, and how to deliver it to the State Personnel Board; go to  spb.colorado.gov ; contact the State Personnel Board for assistance at (303) 866-3300; or refer to 4 Colorado Code of Regulations (CCR) 801-1, State Personnel Board Rules and Personnel Director's Administrative Procedures, Chapter 8, Resolution of Appeals and Disputes, at  spb.colorado.gov  under Rules. SUPPLEMENTAL INFORMATION: RESIDENCY REQUIRMENT Our state constitution requires that applicants for classified positions must be current residents of Colorado AT THE TIME OF APPLICATION.   COMPARATIVE ANALYSIS PROCESS Please be aware the application review is based solely upon the information provided in your application. Therefore, it is imperative that you provide extensive detail in these sections of your application. You should specifically address how, and in what capacity, your qualifications satisfy the minimum requirements of this position. ADAAA ACCOMMODATIONS The State of Colorado believes that equity, diversity, and inclusion drive our success, and we encourage candidates from all identities, backgrounds, and abilities to apply. The State of Colorado is an equal opportunity employer committed to building inclusive, innovative work environments with employees who reflect our communities and enthusiastically serve them. Therefore, in all aspects of the employment process, we provide employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, pregnancy, medical condition related to pregnancy, creed, ancestry, national origin, marital status, genetic information, or military status (with preference given to military veterans), or any other protected status in accordance with applicable law.   Western Colorado University is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. As part of this commitment, Western will assist individuals who have a disability with any reasonable accommodation requests related to employment, including completing the application process, interviewing, completing any pre-employment testing, participating in the employee selection process, and/or performing essential job functions where the requested accommodation does not impose an undue hardship. If you have a disability and require reasonable accommodation to ensure you have a positive experience applying or interviewing for this position, please direct your inquiries to the Office of Human Resources at  HR@western.edu  or (970) 943-3140. THE STATE OF COLORADO IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER Methods of Appointment:  Appointment to the vacancy or vacancies represented by this announcement is expected to be from the eligible list created. However, at the discretion of the appointing authority, the position(s) may be filled by another method of appointment for a valid articulated business reason. Please note the eligible list derived from this announcement may be used to fill more than one vacancy. Primary Physical Work Address: Western Colorado University, 1 Western Way, Gunnison, CO, 81231 Hiring Base Pay Rate: $19.39 per hour FLSA Status: Non-Exempt; position is eligible for overtime compensation. Department Contact Information: Office of Campus Security, Matt Da Silva: (970) 943-3084, mdasilva@western.edu Western Colorado University believes that equity, diversity, and inclusion drive our success, and we encourage candidates from all identities, backgrounds, and abilities to apply. Western is an equal opportunity employer committed to building inclusive, innovative work environments with employees who reflect our communities and enthusiastically serve them. Therefore, in all aspects of the employment process, we provide employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, pregnancy, medical condition related to pregnancy, creed, ancestry, national origin, marital status, genetic information, or military status (for state classified positions, with preference given to military veterans), or any other protected status in accordance with applicable law. Please see our diversity statement, and our DEII Committee charge.   ADAAA ACCOMMODATIONS: Western Colorado University is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. As part of this commitment, Western will assist individuals who have a disability with any reasonable accommodation requests related to employment, including completing the application process, interviewing, completing any pre-employment testing, participating in the employee selection process, and/or performing essential job functions where the requested accommodation does not impose an undue hardship. If you have a disability and require reasonable accommodation to ensure you have a positive experience applying or interviewing for this position, please direct your inquiries to the Office of Human Resources at HR@western.edu or (970) 943-3140. WESTERN COLORADO UNIVERSITY IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER INCLUDING DISABILITY/VETERANS"
    }
